  ("How much does furnace repair cost in Hamilton?", "Furnace repair in Hamilton is quoted in writing after diagnosis, because the price depends on the part. Ignitors, flame sensors and capacitors sit at the low end; blower motors, inducers and control boards cost more. If replacement makes more sense, a new high-efficiency furnace starts at $3,300 installed."),
  ("Can you repair my furnace tonight if it stops during a cold snap?", "We take emergency furnace repair calls in Hamilton on evenings, weekends and holidays. Call 1-647-694-5845, tell us the symptom and where you are, and we'll tell you honestly when a technician can get there."),
  ("Why does my furnace on the Mountain shut off when it's windy?", "A high-efficiency furnace whose intake or exhaust pipe faces the wind can lose pressure or fill with blown snow, and the pressure switch shuts it down. Clearing the terminations restores heat; extending or re-routing the vent keeps it from happening again."),
  ("Is it worth fixing a furnace in a 100-year-old Hamilton house?", "Usually yes, if the furnace itself is under about 12 years old and the chimney or venting is sound. The age of the house matters less than the age of the furnace and the condition of the flue. We check both on the first visit and quote repair and replacement side by side."),
  ("Do you do furnace tune-ups in Hamilton as well as repairs?", "Yes. An annual fall tune-up cleans the burners and flame sensor, tests the safeties and inspects the heat exchanger, and most manufacturers require it to keep extended warranty coverage valid. Ask for tune-up pricing when you call."),
